From c1ba0fe3ff2d0655eb4209d51ce610a63b2e7e8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:52:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(build): the catalog timing line is one write, and the
 contract test runs its two cases in order

The post-merge run 44780029308 failed in
contract::two_broken_cases_report_both_names_and_times. The inner run
started the two broken cases in parallel. The timing line of `within`
went to stderr in pieces, and the panic message of the other case thread
fell between them, so the assert did not find
`catalog <case> <action> elapsed=`.

- support.rs: `timing_line` makes the whole line; `within` writes it with
  one `write_all` on the locked stderr. New pin
  `timing_line_is_one_whole_line`.
- contract.rs: the inner run uses `--test-threads=1`. The asserts stay.

Fixes #3043

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
